1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:05,404
You look up a new phrase.
An hour later, it has vanished.

2
00:00:05,583 --> 00:00:10,646
Try this short routine the next time
you hear a useful expression.

3
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:15,155
Imagine a friend feels overwhelmed
by a long assignment.

4
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:21,462
You say, “Take it one step at a time.
Start with the first question.”

5
00:00:21,625 --> 00:00:27,944
Here, the phrase means focusing on one
small action instead of the whole task.

6
00:00:28,125 --> 00:00:33,194
Now close the subtitles and try to
recall the phrase without looking.

7
00:00:33,375 --> 00:00:38,487
If you get stuck, picture your friend
and that unfinished assignment.

8
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:44,359
Then use the phrase in a different
situation, like a team presentation.

9
00:00:44,542 --> 00:00:49,412
We can take it one step at a time
and make the outline today.

10
00:00:49,583 --> 00:00:54,804
The next day, say the phrase again
and make one more example.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,140
Remember when the phrase fits,
so you can use it when you need it.
